        "text": "- The `typescript` tool's `present` field handles every stored call and result a host passes it (#372). A call with no label and blank code gets a title (its `functionId`, or `typescript`) instead of an empty one, which pi-action rejected. A `saveOnly` result without a saved name shows the `functionId` or the declared function's name, or no summary, instead of `saved undefined`. Results without Pit's details, such as those pi-durable writes itself, and arguments whose `code` isn't a string, are shown by their text instead of throwing.",
