        "anchor": "101:AwY2C",
        "column": 106,
        "text": "- `pit/durable` exports Pit's `typescript` tool for hosts built on `@earendil-works/pi-durable`, such as pi-action. `createPitDurableExtension({ cwd, agentDir, trustProject, ui, log })`, also exported as `createPiDurableExtension` and listed under `pi.durable` in `package.json`, returns an extension with the tool and prompt sections for its guidelines and the user and project function catalogs. Session functions are conversation entries, so a reopened Harness and forks keep them; nested `tools.*` calls go through the host's `executeTool()` and reach every other callable tool, including pi-durable's coding tools, and questions (`ui.*` and the confirmations `functions.*` asks for) work on asynchronous hosts: Pit answers them from a `ui.answer` entry in the conversation or posts them through the host's `ui.ask` and ends the turn, so nothing waits for a person. Interactive hosts can still pass blocking dialogs, during which the program deadline pauses. Project trust is off by default, project function promotion and removal ask through the host's dialogs (and fail without them), and `session.*`, `commands.*`, `models.set`, model requests, and `workspace.viewImage` report that they are unavailable. The entry loads without Pi's coding agent, Pi's TUI, or TypeBox, and `@earendil-works/pi-durable` is an optional peer dependency. See [Pit on pi-durable hosts](docs/durable.md).",
        "before": [
          {
            "line": 100,
            "anchor": "100:AJdNE",
            "text": "- `session.*` on pi-durable hosts: `outline`, `inspectEntry`, `elide`, and `summarize` rewrite the conversation's context with pi-durable edits, and `setNote`/`notes` keep notes in a conversation document shown as the `pit_notes` section, which pi-durable re-sends after compaction and forks inherit. As on Pi, a change applies only if its call succeeds, after the current tool round with `when: \"now\"` and notes, and by default when the run answers, through an `afterRun` hook. See [Context editing and notes](docs/durable.md#context-editing-and-notes)."
