        "line": 87,
        "anchor": "87:4dSKY",
        "column": 104,
        "text": "The `typescript` tool also carries a `present` field for hosts that show tool calls in a log, such as [pi-action's workflow log](https://github.com/cv/pi-action/blob/main/docs/extensions.md#show-tool-calls-in-the-workflow-log). pi-durable ignores it. `present.call(args)` gives the call's title, the label from the `// @pit:` header or the `label` argument (else the program's first line, the `functionId`, or `typescript`), and a body: the program without the header, then `params` as JSON, `functionId`, and `saveOnly`. `present.result(args, result)` gives a summary, the functions the program injected such as `workspace.read · git.status` (`saved <name>` for `saveOnly`, `asked: <title>` for a question, the error's first line on failure), and a body: the returned value with string fields as they are and other values as indented JSON, or the error. Both accept any stored arguments and results, including results pi-durable wrote itself without Pit's details.",
